{
  "plugin": "ufc-scoreboard",
  "_comment": "UFC keeps its three managers as plain attributes -- ufc_live, ufc_recent, ufc_upcoming -- built only when ufc.enabled is set. Its card is fighter-shaped rather than team-shaped: the renderer indexes fighter1_name/fighter2_name, fighter1_id/fighter2_id and fighter1_image_path/fighter2_image_path with [], so a missing key renders blank, and it also reads fight_class, period_text and status_text. period_text is what mma.py builds -- R1..R5 while live, Final once over. No fighter headshots ship with the plugin (they are downloaded from ESPN on first sight), so these renders show the generated placeholder in their place. Fighters, records and odds are invented.",
  "defaults": {
    "width": 128,
    "height": 32,
    "scale": 6,
    "freeze_time": "2026-06-21T02:00:00+00:00",
    "skip_update": true,
    "config": {
      "enabled": true,
      "ufc": {
        "enabled": true
      }
    }
  },
